From f722b37f7582c4f51e175f51e97e8559fcbe0c15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sneezeparty <38020091+sneezeparty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:49:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] plugins/screencast: Only repaint desktop streams for
 their own windows

A desktop stream painted again for every change to any window on any
desktop. It now does so only when the windows it shows, or one of them,
changed. Short-lived windows that are on every desktop (notifications,
on-screen displays, applet popups) and windows hidden by "show desktop"
are left out.

The windows are no longer watched, and so no longer kept drawing, while
the screens are off. With several screens the stream is not held back
for a fullscreen window anymore, since whoever shows it may be on
another screen; the pager pauses its streams itself when it is covered.

The wallpaper lookup only reads the applets file again when that file
changed. A stream_desktop request for an output that is gone fails
rather than falling back to the whole workspace, and oversized sizes
are clamped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
